  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116142",
      "title": "Using the OnPush Strategy",
      "lectureOrder": 199,
      "videoOrder": 191,
      "sourceHash": "603a2069844d8e3b8b858c7c8fb0d128d5d4ad5e928444127305d3e7775aeb13",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "So, avoiding expensive function calls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 7.59,
          "en": "and potentially opting out of zone.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.59,
          "end": 9.21,
          "en": "and therefore change detection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.21,
          "end": 13.143,
          "en": "with certain pieces of your code can be helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.19,
          "end": 18.33,
          "en": "But there is an even more powerful strategy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.33,
          "end": 21.21,
          "en": "you can use in your Angular applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.21,
          "end": 25.02,
          "en": "which can tremendously improve the performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.02,
          "end": 28.41,
          "en": "of your applications depending on how you use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.41,
          "end": 31.5,
          "en": "and how your application is structured.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.5,
          "end": 35.64,
          "en": "Because besides this default strategy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.64,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "where for every event everything is checked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 42.66,
          "en": "for changes in the entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.66,
          "end": 45.06,
          "en": "Besides this strategy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.06,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "Angular also has an alternative change detection strategy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "called the OnPush strategy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 55.59,
          "en": "And this is a opt-in strategy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.59,
          "end": 59.7,
          "en": "which you can enable on a per component basis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.7,
          "end": 62.31,
          "en": "to make sure that change detection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.31,
          "end": 67.31,
          "en": "potentially runs less often for the given component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.65,
          "end": 68.58,
          "en": "So let's enable it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 71.22,
          "en": "and let's then understand how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.22,
          "end": 74.91,
          "en": "Here, I'll go to the MessagesComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.91,
          "end": 77.4,
          "en": "which is the component that outputs the new message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.4,
          "end": 79.68299999999999,
          "en": "and the MessagesListComponents in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 82.35,
          "en": "And in that MessagesComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.35,
          "end": 85.77,
          "en": "I'll opt into this OnPush strategy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.77,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "by going to this decorator configuration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 94.2,
          "en": "and there you can set the changeDetection property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.2,
          "end": 95.913,
          "en": "to ChangeDetectionStrategy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.44,
          "end": 102.363,
          "en": "which is an enum that must be imported from Angular Core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 105.947,
          "en": "ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 109.189,
          "end": 112.56,
          "en": "The default is, you guessed it, the default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.56,
          "end": 115.8,
          "en": "but OnPush is now that opt-in mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.8,
          "end": 119.07,
          "en": "that can be more efficient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 122.34,
          "en": "and we can see the effect of this strategy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.34,
          "end": 126.63,
          "en": "when using it here in the MessagesComponent right away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 126.63,
          "end": 130.14,
          "en": "If I reload my application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.14,
          "end": 133.62,
          "en": "and I wait for that reset counter to occur,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.62,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "which resets my count value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 138.78,
          "en": "you see I still got a lot of logs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.78,
          "end": 140.67000000000002,
          "en": "but if you take a closer look,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.67000000000002,
          "end": 145.022,
          "en": "there isn't a single log from the MessagesComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.022,
          "end": 149.547,
          "en": "the NewMessageComponent or the MessagesListComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.547,
          "end": 150.72,
          "en": "And the same is the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.72,
          "end": 154.17000000000002,
          "en": "if I increment or decrement the counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.17000000000002,
          "end": 156.72,
          "en": "And let's compare that to what we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.72,
          "end": 158.61,
          "en": "with the default strategy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.61,
          "end": 160.38,
          "en": "which you don't need to set by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.38,
          "end": 161.703,
          "en": "since it's the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 165,
          "en": "But here I will set it temporarily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165,
          "end": 167.55,
          "en": "And if I do use that default strategy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.55,
          "end": 171.153,
          "en": "you'll see that now as that counter expires here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.38,
          "end": 177.273,
          "en": "we got logs from Messages, NewMessage and MessagesList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.07,
          "end": 183.633,
          "en": "And these logs are missing when using OnPush.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.83,
          "end": 186.81,
          "en": "If we use that strategy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.81,
          "end": 189.81,
          "en": "and again, we wait for that counter to expire,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.81,
          "end": 193.593,
          "en": "you'll see that logs from these components are missing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.49,
          "end": 197.4,
          "en": "And why is that the case?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 197.4,
          "end": 199.563,
          "en": "What does OnPush do?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
